{"description": "Crawls a document folder, fingerprints every file and diffs it against the RAG ingestion ledger; outputs the document inventory for the RAG ingestion flow.", "displayName": "RAG - List Documents.step", "flowMetadata": {"inputPorts": [], "outputPorts": [{"name": "_rgls_inventory", "displayName": "_rgls_inventory", "minEntries": 1, "maxEntries": 1, "columnDelta": null, "type": "table"}]}, "metadataVersion": 1, "name": "RAG - List Documents.step", "properties": {}, "templates": {"SAS": "/******************************************************************************\n * Copyright \u00a9 2026, SAS Institute Inc., Cary, NC, USA.  All Rights Reserved.\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n *\n * RAG - List Documents: crawl a document source, fingerprint every file\n * (streaming SHA-256) and diff against the incremental-ingestion ledger\n * (the promoted CAS table <project>_LEDGER in the tables caslib).\n * Outputs the document inventory that chains through the RAG flow.\n * Thin shell over rag_core.steps.run_list - see the About tab.\n ******************************************************************************/\n%macro _rgls_setup;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgls_ragProject) %then %global _rgls_ragProject;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgls_tablesCaslib) %then %global _rgls_tablesCaslib;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgls_tablesCaslib)) EQ 0 %then %let _rgls_tablesCaslib = casuser;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgls_configHash) %then %global _rgls_configHash;\n%mend _rgls_setup;\n%_rgls_setup;\n/* Pipeline-wide state, shared by every RAG step in this session.\n   RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR: 1 (default) stops a SAS Studio Flow at the failing\n   step, which is what an interactive user wants. A SCHEDULED run sets it to\n   0: an aborted session never sends SAS Job Execution its completion\n   handshake, so the job would report running forever and its dead compute\n   server would keep counting against the context's server limit.\n   RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED: set by the step that fails; later steps then skip\n   their work and pass the inventory through, so the flow finishes tidily\n   instead of loading half a corpus. A step that starts a chain (List\n   Documents, Purge Documents, Retrieve Context) clears it again.\n   RAG_JOB_FAILED: set by the step that fails as well, and cleared by no\n   step. A job generated from a flow tests it at its end: the flag above\n   may have been cleared by a later chain of the same flow by then. */\n%macro _rag_pipeline_state;\n    %if not %symexist(RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR) %then %do;\n        %global RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR;\n        %let RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR = 1;\n    %end;\n    %if %length(%superq(RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR = 1;\n    %if not %symexist(RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED) %then %global RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED;\n    %if %length(%superq(RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED = 0;\n%mend _rag_pipeline_state;\n%_rag_pipeline_state;\n\n%let _rgls_viyaHost = %sysfunc(getoption(SERVICESBASEURL));\n%let _rgls_rc = 1;\n%let _rgls_state = run;\n%let _rgls_error = The Python program did not run.;\n%let _rgls_summary = ;\n%let _rgls_nrows = 0;\n\n%macro _rgls_guard;\n    %let RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED = 0;\n%mend _rgls_guard;\n%_rgls_guard;\n%macro _rgls_port_default;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgls_inventory) %then %global _rgls_inventory;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgls_inventory)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let _rgls_inventory = rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._INV_LIST;\n%mend _rgls_port_default;\n%_rgls_port_default;\n/* One CAS session for the whole step: created here, reused by\n   SWAT inside proc python, promote+save done by proc casutil.\n   rglsout is where the step's OUTPUT TABLE lands by default -\n   the same caslib as the pipeline tables, so a flow leaves its\n   intermediate results next to each other. */\ncas rglscas uuidmac=_rgls_casuuid;\n%let _rgls_cashost = %sysfunc(getoption(CASHOST));\n%let _rgls_casport = %sysfunc(getoption(CASPORT));\nlibname rglsout cas caslib=\"&_rgls_tablesCaslib.\" sessref=rglscas;\n\n/* A pipeline table that was saved but is not in memory - which is how a CAS\n   server restart leaves every one of them - is loaded back before anything\n   looks at it. The code below only ever tests the in-memory table, so a\n   saved table that is not loaded would read as no previous run at all:\n   every document new, the whole corpus embedded again, and the saved file\n   overwritten by the result.\n   Nothing is done for a table that is in memory or was never saved. A saved\n   file that cannot be loaded FAILS the run, through the caller's state and\n   error variables, because carrying on would destroy what the file holds. */\n%macro _rag_reload_saved(sessref, caslib, table, statevar, errorvar);\n    %local _rag_reload_outcome _rag_reload_syscc;\n    %if %superq(&statevar.) NE run %then %return;\n    %let _rag_reload_outcome = unknown;\n    %let _rag_reload_syscc = &syscc.;\n    proc cas;\n        session &sessref.;\n        outcome = \"memory\";\n        table.tableExists result = found / caslib = \"&caslib.\" name = \"&table.\";\n        if found.exists == 0 then do;\n            /* The saved file carries the table name as it was typed and a\n               path-based caslib is case-sensitive, while CAS table names\n               are not - so the file is looked up in the listing: the exact\n               name when there is one, otherwise the same name in another\n               case. */\n            outcome = \"absent\";\n            saved = \"\";\n            table.fileInfo result = listing status = listed / caslib = \"&caslib.\";\n            if listed.severity == 0 then do;\n                if exists(listing, \"FileInfo\") then do;\n                    do entry over listing.FileInfo;\n                        if entry.Name == \"&table..sashdat\" then\n                            saved = entry.Name;\n                        else if saved == \"\" and upcase(entry.Name) == upcase(\"&table..sashdat\") then\n                            saved = entry.Name;\n                    end;\n                end;\n            end;\n            else outcome = \"unlisted\";\n            if saved != \"\" then do;\n                table.loadTable result = ignored status = loaded / caslib = \"&caslib.\" path = saved\n                    casOut = {caslib = \"&caslib.\", name = \"&table.\", promote = true};\n                /* A concurrent session may have loaded the table in the\n                   meantime. That refuses this load, and is just as good. */\n                table.tableExists result = found / caslib = \"&caslib.\" name = \"&table.\";\n                if found.exists != 0 then outcome = \"loaded\";\n                else outcome = \"failed\";\n            end;\n        end;\n        /* \"L\": the macro variable is local to this macro, and without a\n           scope CASL writes to the global symbol table */\n        call symputx(\"_rag_reload_outcome\", outcome, \"L\");\n    quit;\n    /* Looking is not part of the run and never decides its condition code:\n       not a load that was refused because another session got there first,\n       and not a load that failed either - that one is reported through the\n       caller's state, the way the caller reports every other failure. */\n    %let syscc = &_rag_reload_syscc.;\n    %if &_rag_reload_outcome. EQ failed %then %do;\n        %let &statevar. = fail;\n        /* one line: the caller writes it to the log as its ERROR line */\n        %let &errorvar. = the saved table &caslib..&table. could not be loaded into memory (CAS messages above) - stopped, because an empty table would re-embed the corpus and overwrite the saved file;\n        %return;\n    %end;\n    /* The run goes on in the two cases that are left, and says what that\n       means. unlisted: the table is not in memory and the files of the caslib\n       could not be listed, so no saved copy was looked for - the case the\n       reload is there for, without the reload. Anything else: PROC CAS ended\n       before it handed back an outcome, and not even that much is known. */\n    %if &_rag_reload_outcome. EQ loaded %then\n        %put NOTE: RAG: &caslib..&table. was saved but not in memory and has been loaded from its saved file.;\n    %else %if &_rag_reload_outcome. EQ unlisted %then %do;\n        %put WARNING: RAG: &caslib..&table. is not in memory, and the files of the caslib &caslib. could not be listed (CAS messages above) - a saved copy could not be looked for.;\n        %put WARNING: RAG: the run continues without the table and saves over a copy that may be there. A ledger that is not in memory means that every document counts as new and is embedded again.;\n    %end;\n    %else %if &_rag_reload_outcome. NE memory and &_rag_reload_outcome. NE absent %then %do;\n        %put WARNING: RAG: could not look for &caslib..&table. - PROC CAS ended before it said whether the table is in memory or saved (messages above). The run continues with what is in memory.;\n        %put WARNING: RAG: if the table is not in memory, the run saves over a copy that may be there. A ledger that is not in memory means that every document counts as new and is embedded again.;\n    %end;\n%mend _rag_reload_saved;\n%_rag_reload_saved(rglscas, &_rgls_tablesCaslib., &_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER, _rgls_state, _rgls_error);\n\n/* ---- One ledger, two writers ----------------------------------------------\n   The ledger is written by the RAG steps and by the single-program job\n   Ingest-Documents.sas, and the two do not leave it alike: the Load and Purge\n   steps upload it through SWAT, which makes its text columns VARCHAR, and\n   the job loads it from a SAS data set, which makes them CHAR. CAS refuses\n   to append a row whose column is the one where the table has the other\n   (The variable doc_id has been specified with incompatible data types -\n   found live, in both directions), so a run lock declared one way could\n   only be written to a ledger the same writer had left.\n   The table is asked what it holds and the lock row is declared to match.\n   doc_id answers for all text columns, because each writer creates all of\n   them the same way. An answer that is neither char nor varchar falls back\n   to what this writer leaves itself, which is what it declared before.\n   The same two macros stand in RAG - List Documents, RAG - Purge Documents\n   and Ingest-Documents.sas; only the prefix of their names differs. */\n%macro _rgls_ledger_types(session, caslib, table, fallback);\n    %global _rgls_ledgerTypes;\n    %let _rgls_ledgerTypes = ;\n    %if %sysfunc(exist(work._rgls_ledger_ci)) %then %do;\n        proc delete data=work._rgls_ledger_ci;\n        run;\n    %end;\n    proc cas;\n        session &session.;\n        table.columnInfo result=_rgls_ci /\n            table={caslib=\"&caslib.\", name=\"&table.\"};\n        saveresult _rgls_ci dataout=work._rgls_ledger_ci;\n    quit;\n    %if %sysfunc(exist(work._rgls_ledger_ci)) %then %do;\n        data _null_;\n            set work._rgls_ledger_ci;\n            if lowcase(strip(Column)) = \"doc_id\" then\n                call symputx(\"_rgls_ledgerTypes\", lowcase(strip(Type)), \"G\");\n        run;\n        proc delete data=work._rgls_ledger_ci;\n        run;\n    %end;\n    %if &_rgls_ledgerTypes. NE char %then %if &_rgls_ledgerTypes. NE varchar %then %do;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"NOTE: the column types of the ledger &caslib..&table. could not be read - the run lock is written as &fallback.\";\n        run;\n        %let _rgls_ledgerTypes = &fallback.;\n        %return;\n    %end;\n    data _null_;\n        putLog \"NOTE: the ledger &caslib..&table. holds its text columns as &_rgls_ledgerTypes. - the run lock is written the same way\";\n    run;\n%mend _rgls_ledger_types;\n/* The LENGTH statement of a ledger row, spelled the way the table holds its\n   text. The char lengths are the ones the job gives its ledger. */\n%macro _rgls_ledger_length;\n    %if &_rgls_ledgerTypes. EQ char %then %do;\n        length doc_id $ 40 source_uri $ 1024 source_kind $ 16\n               content_hash $ 64 mtime $ 32 status $ 12 error_text $ 512\n               pipeline_version $ 32 config_hash $ 32 chunk_count 8\n               run_id $ 32 updated_at $ 24;\n    %end;\n    %else %do;\n        length doc_id varchar(40) source_uri varchar(1024)\n               source_kind varchar(16) content_hash varchar(64)\n               mtime varchar(32) status varchar(12)\n               error_text varchar(512) pipeline_version varchar(32)\n               config_hash varchar(32) chunk_count 8\n               run_id varchar(32) updated_at varchar(24);\n    %end;\n%mend _rgls_ledger_length;\n%macro _rgls_lock;\n    /* %global, not %let: a %let inside a macro makes a LOCAL variable, so the\n       run id would never reach the python block that stamps it on every row */\n    %global _rgls_lockHeld _rgls_runId _rgls_ledgerTypes;\n    %local _rgls_now _rgls_uuid _rgls_digits;\n    %let _rgls_lockHeld = ;\n    %let _rgls_now = %sysevalf(%sysfunc(datetime()) - 315619200);\n    /* run-<epoch>-<digits>. The epoch alone collided: rag_runs is keyed on\n       the run id and shared by every project in the database, so two projects\n       starting in the same second overwrote one another's run and merged\n       their document events. The digits were &sysjobid, and that does not\n       tell two SAS sessions apart: it was 344 in twelve flow runs, each in\n       a compute server of its own, and 343 or 345 in the four other runs\n       (measured live). They are now the first eight hexadecimal digits of a\n       UUID, written as a number of ten digits - UUIDGEN returns another one\n       with every call. Where it returns none, the digits are &sysjobid as\n       before. */\n    %let _rgls_digits = &sysjobid.;\n    %let _rgls_uuid = %sysfunc(uuidgen());\n    %if %length(&_rgls_uuid.) GE 8 %then\n        %let _rgls_digits = %sysfunc(inputn(%substr(&_rgls_uuid., 1, 8), hex8.), z10.);\n    %let _rgls_runId = run-%sysfunc(compress(%sysfunc(putn(&_rgls_now., 12.))))-&_rgls_digits.;\n    %if &_rgls_state. NE run %then %return;\n    %if %sysfunc(exist(rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER)) %then %do;\n        /* The newest lock row decides. A ledger can hold more than one: the\n           row of a run that crashed stays until a run that goes through\n           writes the ledger. The row that was read last was taken, which is\n           no particular one, and a stale row then hid the fresh lock of a\n           run that is at work. A time that cannot be read is no lock. */\n        data _null_;\n            set rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER(where=(doc_id = \"__run_lock__\"));\n            retain newest;\n            taken = input(mtime, ?? best32.);\n            if taken > newest then do;\n                newest = taken;\n                call symputx(\"_rgls_lockHeld\", newest, \"G\");\n            end;\n        run;\n    %end;\n    %if %length(&_rgls_lockHeld.) GT 0 %then %do;\n        %if %sysevalf(&_rgls_now. - &_rgls_lockHeld. < 1800) %then %do;\n            %let _rgls_state = fail;\n            %let _rgls_error = another ingestion run holds the lock on this ledger - wait for it to finish, or retry in 30 minutes if it crashed;\n            %return;\n        %end;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"NOTE: RAG - List Documents: a stale run lock (held longer than 30 minutes) is ignored\";\n        run;\n    %end;\n    /* take it: append when the ledger exists, otherwise start it */\n    %if %sysfunc(exist(rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER)) %then %do;\n        %_rgls_ledger_types(rglscas, &_rgls_tablesCaslib., &_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER, varchar);\n        data rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER(append=yes);\n            %_rgls_ledger_length\n            doc_id = \"__run_lock__\";\n            mtime = strip(put(&_rgls_now., best20.));\n            status = \"lock\";\n            run_id = \"&_rgls_runId.\";\n            source_uri = \"\"; source_kind = \"\"; content_hash = \"\";\n            error_text = \"\"; pipeline_version = \"\"; config_hash = \"\";\n            chunk_count = 0; updated_at = \"\";\n        run;\n    %end;\n    %else %do;\n        proc casutil sessref=rglscas\n                     incaslib=\"&_rgls_tablesCaslib.\"\n                     outcaslib=\"&_rgls_tablesCaslib.\";\n            droptable casdata=\"&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER\" quiet;\n        quit;\n        /* no ledger yet: it starts the way the steps leave one, as varchar */\n        %let _rgls_ledgerTypes = varchar;\n        data rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER(promote=yes);\n            %_rgls_ledger_length\n            doc_id = \"__run_lock__\";\n            mtime = strip(put(&_rgls_now., best20.));\n            status = \"lock\";\n            run_id = \"&_rgls_runId.\";\n            source_uri = \"\"; source_kind = \"\"; content_hash = \"\";\n            error_text = \"\"; pipeline_version = \"\"; config_hash = \"\";\n            chunk_count = 0; updated_at = \"\";\n        run;\n    %end;\n    /* a lock that failed to write is not a lock: refuse rather than let a\n       second ingestion interleave unguarded */\n    %let _rgls_lockHeld = ;\n    data _null_;\n        set rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER(where=(doc_id = \"__run_lock__\" and run_id = \"&_rgls_runId.\"));\n        call symputx(\"_rgls_lockHeld\", run_id, \"G\");\n    run;\n    %if %length(&_rgls_lockHeld.) EQ 0 %then %do;\n        %let _rgls_state = fail;\n        %let _rgls_error = the run lock could not be written to &_rgls_tablesCaslib..&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER - refusing to ingest unguarded;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgls_lock;\n%_rgls_lock;\nproc python restart;\nsubmit;\ndef main():\n    import json\n    import os\n    import sys\n    import tempfile\n    import time\n    import traceback\n\n    # nothing to do when the step is only passing the inventory through\n    if str(SAS.symget(\"_rgls_state\") or \"run\").strip() != \"run\":\n        return\n\n    def sas_safe(text):\n        \"\"\"Strings crossing into SAS.logMessage/SAS.symput are embedded into\n        generated SAS statements - quotes and macro characters corrupt the\n        code stream (verified live). EVERY such string goes through here.\"\"\"\n        # Each such character becomes one that reads the same, as in the\n        # logging programs: the setup`s window, 85pct, R+D. A blank in its\n        # place lost what the message said. The two comment marks are put\n        # together from their halves, so that this block holds neither.\n        cleaned = str(text)\n        for bad, good in ((\"'\", \"`\"), ('\"', \"`\"), (\"%\", \"pct \"), (\"&\", \"+\"),\n                          (\";\", \",\"), (\"/\" + \"*\", \"/ *\"), (\"*\" + \"/\", \"* /\")):\n            cleaned = cleaned.replace(bad, good)\n        return cleaned\n\n    def M(msg):\n        SAS.logMessage(\"RAGLIST \" + sas_safe(msg))\n\n    try:\n        import requests\n    except Exception:\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgls_error\", \"The Python environment of this compute \"\n                                   \"context lacks the requests package - see \"\n                                   \"the RAG administration guide.\")\n        return\n    try:\n        import pandas as pd\n        import swat\n    except Exception:\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgls_error\", \"The Python environment of this compute \"\n                                   \"context lacks the swat/pandas packages \"\n                                   \"required for the CAS table transport - \"\n                                   \"see the RAG administration guide.\")\n        return\n\n    BASE = str(SAS.symget(\"_rgls_viyaHost\") or \"\").rstrip(\"/\")\n    TOKEN = os.environ.get(\"SAS_SERVICES_TOKEN\", \"\")\n    AUTH = {\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + TOKEN}\n    VERIFY = os.environ.get(\"SSLCALISTLOC\") or os.environ.get(\"CAS_CLIENT_SSL_CA_LIST\") or True\n    WORKPATH = SAS.workpath if SAS.workpath.endswith(os.sep) else SAS.workpath + os.sep\n\n    P = {name: str(SAS.symget(name) or \"\").strip() for name in [\n        \"_rgls_sourcePath\",\n        \"_rgls_pipelineVersion\",\n        \"_rgls_includeCode\",\n        \"_rgls_configHash\",\n        \"_rgls_runId\",\n        \"_rgls_ragProject\",\n        \"_rgls_tablesCaslib\",\n        \"_rgls_ragCorePath\",\n    ]}\n\n    def read_rows(filename, missing_message):\n        path = WORKPATH + filename\n        if not os.path.exists(path):\n            raise RuntimeError(missing_message)\n        with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            data = json.load(fh)\n        rows = []\n        for row in data if isinstance(data, list) else []:\n            rows.append({str(k).lower(): v for k, v in row.items()})\n        return rows\n\n    def multiline(control):\n        \"\"\"Every line a user typed into a multi-line text field.\"\"\"\n        # SAS Studio splits such a field for us: it emits <control>_count and\n        # <control>_1..N, and leaves the plain macro variable holding only the\n        # FIRST line. Reading just the plain one silently turned two questions\n        # into one run-on question (found live in a flow). Semicolons are still\n        # accepted, for callers that set the parameter directly.\n        values = []\n        try:\n            count = int(float(SAS.symget(control + \"_count\") or 0))\n        except Exception:\n            count = 0\n        if count > 0:\n            for index in range(1, count + 1):\n                try:\n                    piece = str(SAS.symget(\"%s_%d\" % (control, index)) or \"\")\n                except Exception:\n                    piece = \"\"\n                if piece.strip():\n                    values.append(piece.strip())\n            if values:\n                return values\n        raw = str(P.get(control) or \"\").replace(\";\", \"\\n\")\n        return [line.strip() for line in raw.split(\"\\n\") if line.strip()]\n\n    def clean_path(raw):\n        \"\"\"Path-selector values arrive scheme-prefixed (sasserver:/...,\n        sascontent:/...); strip the scheme off.\"\"\"\n        value = str(raw or \"\").strip()\n        for scheme in (\"sascontent:\", \"sasserver:\"):\n            if value.lower().startswith(scheme):\n                return value[len(scheme):]\n        return value\n\n    STARTED = time.time()\n    SUMMARY = []\n\n    def summarize(line):\n        \"\"\"One line of the step's log summary (SAS prints them at the end).\"\"\"\n        SUMMARY.append(str(line))\n\n    def publish_summary(target):\n        elapsed = time.time() - STARTED\n        summarize(f\"elapsed {elapsed:.1f}s\")\n        SAS.symput(target, sas_safe(\" | \".join(SUMMARY))[:1500])\n\n    def write_rows(filename, rows, columns, numeric=()):\n        out = []\n        for row in rows:\n            rec = {}\n            for column in columns:\n                value = row.get(column)\n                if column in numeric:\n                    try:\n                        rec[column] = float(value or 0)\n                    except Exception:\n                        rec[column] = 0.0\n                else:\n                    rec[column] = \"\" if value is None else str(value)\n            out.append(rec)\n        with open(WORKPATH + filename, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            json.dump(out, fh)\n        return len(out)\n\n    try:\n        # ---- CAS: reuse the session the step created in SAS ---------------\n        # (sas-studio-custom-steps: Reuse-CAS-session-from-SWAT)\n        import re as _re\n        os.environ.setdefault(\"CAS_CLIENT_SSL_CA_LIST\",\n                              os.environ.get(\"SSLCALISTLOC\", \"\"))\n        try:\n            conn = swat.CAS(hostname=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgls_cashost\") or \"\"),\n                            port=int(float(SAS.symget(\"_rgls_casport\") or 5570)),\n                            password=TOKEN,\n                            session=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgls_casuuid\") or \"\"))\n        except Exception as exc:\n            # The step reuses the CAS session SAS created, because the staged\n            # table has to be visible to the casutil promote that follows. CAS\n            # only lets an identity reconnect to its OWN session, and a context\n            # that runs the server as a service account breaks that: SAS and\n            # its token are the service account while the CAS session belongs\n            # to the user who launched the job.\n            #\n            # SWAT's exception says only \"Could not connect ... on port 5570\";\n            # the server's real message (\"Users can only reconnect to their own\n            # sessions\") goes to stderr and never reaches the exception, so\n            # matching on text does not work. Connecting WITHOUT the session id\n            # separates the two causes: if that works, CAS is reachable and the\n            # problem is whose session it is.\n            reachable = False\n            try:\n                probe = swat.CAS(\n                    hostname=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgls_cashost\") or \"\"),\n                    port=int(float(SAS.symget(\"_rgls_casport\") or 5570)),\n                    password=TOKEN)\n                reachable = True\n                probe.close()\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n            if reachable:\n                raise RuntimeError(\n                    \"this compute context cannot run the RAG steps: CAS is \"\n                    \"reachable, but the SAS session and the CAS session belong \"\n                    \"to different identities, so the step cannot reuse the CAS \"\n                    \"session it needs. The stock 'SAS Job Execution compute \"\n                    \"context' has this problem because it runs the server as a \"\n                    \"service account. Run the job in a context that runs as the \"\n                    \"REQUESTING USER - the 'SAS Studio compute context' does, \"\n                    \"and a full flow was verified there. See the RAG \"\n                    \"administration guide.\")\n            raise\n        CASLIB = P[\"_rgls_tablesCaslib\"] or \"casuser\"\n        if not _re.match(r\"^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,19}$\",\n                         P[\"_rgls_ragProject\"] or \"\"):\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                \"ragProject must be 1-20 characters (letters, digits, \"\n                \"underscores, starting with a letter) so every \"\n                \"project_suffix table name stays within the 32 characters \"\n                \"SAS Studio displays\")\n\n        def project_table(suffix):\n            return P[\"_rgls_ragProject\"] + suffix\n\n        def stamp(rows):\n            \"\"\"Every inventory row names its pipeline, so the next step\n            inherits the project and caslib instead of asking again.\"\"\"\n            for row in rows:\n                row[\"rag_project\"] = P[\"_rgls_ragProject\"]\n                row[\"tables_caslib\"] = CASLIB\n            return rows\n\n        def cas_read(name, required_message=None):\n            \"\"\"Read a pipeline table into lower-cased row dicts; absent\n            table = empty (the pipeline's empty state) unless required.\"\"\"\n            if not conn.table.tableExists(caslib=CASLIB, name=name).exists:\n                if required_message:\n                    raise RuntimeError(required_message)\n                return []\n            frame = conn.CASTable(name, caslib=CASLIB).to_frame()\n            rows = []\n            for record in frame.to_dict(\"records\"):\n                row = {}\n                for key, value in record.items():\n                    row[str(key).lower()] = None if pd.isna(value) else value\n                rows.append(row)\n            return rows\n\n        def ledger_value(value):\n            \"\"\"One value of a ledger row, as the pipeline compares it.\"\"\"\n            # The text columns of the ledger are VARCHAR when the Load step\n            # wrote it and CHAR when the single-program job did, and CAS\n            # stores a CHAR value padded with blanks to the length of its\n            # column. Whether SWAT hands that padding on was not measured,\n            # so it is taken off here: a padded run id is not the id of\n            # this run, and a padded fingerprint is not the fingerprint of\n            # the document.\n            if value is None:\n                return \"\"\n            if isinstance(value, str):\n                return value.rstrip(\" \")\n            return value\n\n        def label_columns(name, columns):\n            \"\"\"Put the shipped column labels on a CAS table - they survive\n            the promote, so the pipeline tables read without the schema.\"\"\"\n            try:\n                from rag_core.steps import column_labels\n                labels = column_labels(columns)\n                if labels:\n                    conn.table.alterTable(\n                        caslib=CASLIB, name=name,\n                        columns=[{\"name\": column, \"label\": label}\n                                 for column, label in labels.items()])\n            except Exception as exc:\n                M(f\"column labels not applied to {name}: {exc}\")\n\n        def cas_stage(name, rows, columns, numeric=()):\n            \"\"\"Upload the session-scope staging table <name>_S with varchar\n            columns (no 32k limit); the SAS side swaps it into the promoted\n            global table and saves it, so the previous state survives a\n            mid-step failure.\"\"\"\n            if not rows:\n                return 0\n            data = []\n            for row in rows:\n                rec = []\n                for column in columns:\n                    value = row.get(column)\n                    if column in numeric:\n                        try:\n                            rec.append(float(value or 0))\n                        except Exception:\n                            rec.append(0.0)\n                    else:\n                        rec.append(\"\" if value is None else str(value))\n                data.append(rec)\n            frame = pd.DataFrame(data, columns=list(columns))\n            spec = [{\"name\": column,\n                     \"type\": \"double\" if column in numeric else \"varchar\"}\n                    for column in columns]\n            conn.upload_frame(frame,\n                              casout={\"name\": name + \"_S\", \"caslib\": CASLIB,\n                                      \"replace\": True},\n                              importoptions={\"fileType\": \"csv\",\n                                             \"allowEmbeddedNewLines\": True,\n                                             \"vars\": spec})\n            label_columns(name + \"_S\", columns)\n            return len(rows)\n\n        # ---- rag_core bootstrap: download the governed SAS Content folder --\n        def get_json(endpoint, **params):\n            response = requests.get(BASE + endpoint, params=params, headers=AUTH,\n                                    verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n            response.raise_for_status()\n            return response.json()\n\n        def download_folder(folder_id, local_dir):\n            os.makedirs(local_dir, exist_ok=True)\n            count = 0\n            members = get_json(f\"/folders/folders/{folder_id}/members\", limit=200)\n            for member in members.get(\"items\", []):\n                uri = member.get(\"uri\", \"\")\n                if \"/files/files/\" in uri:\n                    content = requests.get(BASE + uri + \"/content\", headers=AUTH,\n                                           verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 60))\n                    content.raise_for_status()\n                    with open(os.path.join(local_dir, member[\"name\"]), \"wb\") as fh:\n                        fh.write(content.content)\n                    count += 1\n                elif \"/folders/folders/\" in uri:\n                    count += download_folder(uri.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1],\n                                             os.path.join(local_dir, member[\"name\"]))\n            return count\n\n        core_path = (clean_path(P[\"_rgls_ragCorePath\"])\n                     or \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core\")\n        root = requests.get(BASE + \"/folders/folders/@item\",\n                            params={\"path\": core_path}, headers=AUTH,\n                            verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n        if root.status_code != 200:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"rag_core folder {core_path} not found \"\n                               f\"(HTTP {root.status_code}) - deploy it per the \"\n                               \"administration guide\")\n        staging = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"rag_core_\")\n        n_files = download_folder(root.json()[\"id\"], os.path.join(staging, \"rag_core\"))\n        sys.path.insert(0, staging)\n        import rag_core\n        M(f\"rag_core {rag_core.RAG_CORE_VERSION} bootstrapped ({n_files} files)\")\n\n        from rag_core.sources import make_source\n        from rag_core.steps import (INVENTORY_COLUMNS, LEDGER_COLUMNS, run_list,\n                                    stamp_config)\n\n        inventory_columns = INVENTORY_COLUMNS\n        if not P[\"_rgls_sourcePath\"]:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"pick the folder holding the documents - on \"\n                               \"the compute server file system or in SAS \"\n                               \"Content\")\n        # the selector's scheme decides which source is built\n        source = make_source(P[\"_rgls_sourcePath\"], BASE, TOKEN, VERIFY)\n\n        own_run_id = P[\"_rgls_runId\"]\n        ledger = []\n        for row in cas_read(project_table(\"_LEDGER\")):\n            ledger.append({column: ledger_value(row.get(column))\n                           for column in inventory_columns})\n        real_rows = [r for r in ledger if r.get(\"doc_id\") != \"__run_lock__\"]\n        # own_run_id is set by each step before this block: OUR run's lock is\n        # expected (the first step took it), anyone else's means a concurrent\n        # ingestion is live on this ledger\n        lock_rows = [r for r in ledger\n                     if r.get(\"doc_id\") == \"__run_lock__\"\n                     and str(r.get(\"run_id\") or \"\") != str(own_run_id or \"\")]\n        if lock_rows:\n            # the newest lock decides: the row of a run that crashed can\n            # stand beside the row of a run that is at work, and the first\n            # row is whichever CAS returned first\n            held_for = 1e9\n            for held in lock_rows:\n                try:\n                    held_for = min(held_for,\n                                   time.time() - float(held.get(\"mtime\") or 0))\n                except Exception:\n                    pass\n            if held_for < 1800:\n                raise RuntimeError(\"another ingestion run holds the lock on \"\n                                   \"this ledger - wait for it to finish, or \"\n                                   \"retry in 30 minutes if it crashed\")\n            M(\"stale run lock ignored (held longer than 30 minutes)\")\n\n        run_id = own_run_id or f\"run-{int(time.time())}\"\n        pipeline_version = P[\"_rgls_pipelineVersion\"] or \"v1\"\n        # Same setting the generated job passes as includeCode. Without\n        # it this step defaulted to False, so a setup with \"ingest\n        # source-code files\" ticked listed every .py/.sas as skipped\n        # when it ran as a flow and ingested them when it ran as a job.\n        inventory = run_list(source, real_rows, run_id, pipeline_version,\n                             P[\"_rgls_configHash\"],\n                             include_code=P[\"_rgls_includeCode\"] == \"1\",\n                             log=M)\n        # the pipeline configuration starts here and accumulates down the flow\n        stamp_config(inventory, {\"pipeline_version\": pipeline_version,\n                                 \"source_kind\": source.kind})\n        n_rows = write_rows(\"rgls_inventory_out.json\", stamp(inventory),\n                            inventory_columns, numeric=(\"chunk_count\",))\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgls_nrows\", str(n_rows))\n        counts = {}\n        for row in inventory:\n            counts[row.get(\"status\")] = counts.get(row.get(\"status\"), 0) + 1\n        pending = counts.get(\"new\", 0) + counts.get(\"changed\", 0)\n        summarize(f\"source: {source.describe()}\")\n        summarize(f\"run {run_id}, pipeline version {pipeline_version}\")\n        summarize(f\"ledger read: {len(real_rows)} documents from \"\n                  f\"{CASLIB}.{project_table('_LEDGER')}\")\n        summarize(f\"{n_rows} documents in scope (\"\n                  + \", \".join(f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in sorted(counts.items()))\n                  + \")\")\n        summarize(f\"{pending} continue down the flow, \"\n                  f\"{counts.get('unchanged', 0)} skipped as unchanged\")\n        publish_summary(\"_rgls_summary\")\n\n        try:\n            conn.close(close_session=False)\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgls_rc\", \"0\")\n    except Exception as error:\n        error_text = f\"{type(error).__name__}: {error}\"\n        M(\"failed: \" + sas_safe(error_text))\n        print(traceback.format_exc())\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgls_error\", sas_safe(error_text)[:500])\n\n\nmain()\nendsubmit;\nrun; quit;\nproc python terminate;\nrun; quit;\n\n%macro _rgls_emit_inventory;\n    %if &_rgls_rc. NE 0 %then %return;\n    %local lib table opts;\n    %let lib = %upcase(%scan(&_rgls_inventory., 1, .));\n    %let table = %scan(&_rgls_inventory., 2, .);\n    %if &lib. EQ %upcase(rglsout) %then %do;\n        proc casutil sessref=rglscas\n                     incaslib=\"&_rgls_tablesCaslib.\"\n                     outcaslib=\"&_rgls_tablesCaslib.\";\n            droptable casdata=\"&table.\" quiet;\n        quit;\n        %let opts = (promote=yes);\n    %end;\n    %else %let opts = (compress=yes);\n    %if &_rgls_nrows. GT 0 %then %do;\n        filename rglsino \"%sysfunc(pathname(work))/rgls_inventory_out.json\";\n        libname rglsinj json fileref=rglsino;\n        data &_rgls_inventory.&opts.;\n            length doc_id $ 40 source_uri $ 1024 source_kind $ 16\n                   content_hash $ 64 mtime $ 32 status $ 12 error_text $ 512\n                   pipeline_version $ 32 config_hash $ 32 chunk_count 8\n                   run_id $ 32 updated_at $ 24 extractor $ 64\n                   rag_project $ 20 tables_caslib $ 32 config_json $ 1024\n                   embed_usage $ 32767 enrich_usage $ 32767;\n            label doc_id=\"Document ID\" source_uri=\"Source location\"\n                  source_kind=\"Source type\" content_hash=\"Content fingerprint\"\n                  mtime=\"Source last modified\" status=\"Ingestion status\"\n                  error_text=\"Failure reason\" pipeline_version=\"Pipeline version\"\n                  config_hash=\"Configuration fingerprint\" chunk_count=\"Chunks produced\"\n                  run_id=\"Ingestion run ID\" updated_at=\"Row updated (UTC)\"\n                  extractor=\"Text extractor used\" rag_project=\"RAG project\"\n                  tables_caslib=\"Pipeline tables caslib\"\n                  config_json=\"Pipeline configuration (JSON)\"\n                  embed_usage=\"Embedding usage (JSON)\"\n                  enrich_usage=\"Enrichment usage (JSON)\";\n            set rglsinj.root(drop=ordinal_root);\n        run;\n        libname rglsinj clear;\n        filename rglsino clear;\n    %end;\n    %else %do;\n        data &_rgls_inventory.&opts.;\n            length doc_id $ 40 source_uri $ 1024 source_kind $ 16\n                   content_hash $ 64 mtime $ 32 status $ 12 error_text $ 512\n                   pipeline_version $ 32 config_hash $ 32 chunk_count 8\n                   run_id $ 32 updated_at $ 24 extractor $ 64\n                   rag_project $ 20 tables_caslib $ 32 config_json $ 1024\n                   embed_usage $ 32767 enrich_usage $ 32767;\n            label doc_id=\"Document ID\" source_uri=\"Source location\"\n                  source_kind=\"Source type\" content_hash=\"Content fingerprint\"\n                  mtime=\"Source last modified\" status=\"Ingestion status\"\n                  error_text=\"Failure reason\" pipeline_version=\"Pipeline version\"\n                  config_hash=\"Configuration fingerprint\" chunk_count=\"Chunks produced\"\n                  run_id=\"Ingestion run ID\" updated_at=\"Row updated (UTC)\"\n                  extractor=\"Text extractor used\" rag_project=\"RAG project\"\n                  tables_caslib=\"Pipeline tables caslib\"\n                  config_json=\"Pipeline configuration (JSON)\"\n                  embed_usage=\"Embedding usage (JSON)\"\n                  enrich_usage=\"Enrichment usage (JSON)\";\n            call missing(of _all_);\n            stop;\n        run;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgls_emit_inventory;\n%_rgls_emit_inventory;\n%macro _rgls_release;\n    %local failing held;\n    %let failing = 0;\n    %if &_rgls_state. EQ fail %then %let failing = 1;\n    %if &_rgls_state. EQ run %then %if &_rgls_rc. NE 0 %then %let failing = 1;\n    %if &failing. EQ 0 %then %return;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgls_runId) %then %return;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgls_runId)) EQ 0 %then %return;\n    %if not %sysfunc(exist(rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER)) %then %return;\n    /* Only a run whose own lock row stands in the ledger has a lock to hand\n       back. A run that the fresh lock of another run refused took none, a\n       preview of RAG - Purge Documents takes none, and the row is gone once\n       the run has written its ledger (RAG - Load Vector Store, or a purge).\n       Rewriting the ledger then released nothing: it saved the table again\n       - with the lock of the OTHER run in the file that is loaded back when\n       the table is no longer in memory - and the NOTE below said that a\n       lock had been released. */\n    %let held = ;\n    data _null_;\n        set rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER(where=(doc_id = \"__run_lock__\" and run_id = \"&_rgls_runId.\"));\n        call symputx(\"held\", run_id, \"L\");\n    run;\n    %if %length(&held.) EQ 0 %then %return;\n    data rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER_R(replace=yes);\n        set rglsout.&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER(where=(not (doc_id = \"__run_lock__\"\n                                 and run_id = \"&_rgls_runId.\")));\n    run;\n    proc casutil sessref=rglscas incaslib=\"&_rgls_tablesCaslib.\"\n                 outcaslib=\"&_rgls_tablesCaslib.\";\n        droptable casdata=\"&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER\" quiet;\n        promote casdata=\"&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER_R\"\n                casout=\"&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER\";\n        save casdata=\"&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER\"\n             casout=\"&_rgls_ragProject._LEDGER\" replace;\n    quit;\n    data _null_;\n        putLog \"NOTE: RAG - List Documents: the run lock was released so the run can be retried\";\n    run;\n%mend _rgls_release;\n%_rgls_release;\n\nlibname rglsout clear;\ncas rglscas terminate;\n\n%macro _rgls_status;\n    %if &_rgls_state. EQ run %then %if &_rgls_rc. NE 0 %then\n        %let _rgls_state = fail;\n    %if &_rgls_state. EQ skip %then %do;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"NOTE: ----- RAG - List Documents: skipped -----\";\n        run;\n        %return;\n    %end;\n    %if &_rgls_state. EQ fail %then %do;\n        %let RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED = 1;\n        %global RAG_JOB_FAILED;\n        %let RAG_JOB_FAILED = 1;\n        /* The message is read with symget and the line is put together in\n           a variable, as the summary below is. Written into the program as\n           a quoted string, a message that took the line beyond 262 bytes\n           made SAS write the NOTE that suspects unbalanced quotation marks\n           above the ERROR. 2000 bytes hold the 500 characters the Python\n           block hands over at most. */\n        data _null_;\n            length message $ 2000 line $ 2100;\n            message = symget(\"_rgls_error\");\n            line = \"ERROR: RAG - List Documents failed: \" || message;\n            putLog line;\n        run;\n        %if &RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR. NE 0 %then %do;\n            data _null_;\n                abort 42;\n            run;\n        %end;\n        %return;\n    %end;\n    /* The summary is read with symget and never written into the program\n       as a quoted string. A summary is usually longer than 262 bytes, and\n       a quoted string of that length makes SAS write the NOTE that suspects\n       unbalanced quotation marks - once for each of the two strings that\n       held it here. 6000 bytes hold the 1500 characters the Python block\n       hands over at most.\n       A part is written as one value with its prefix. Written after the\n       prefix as a value of its own, a part that did not fit into the rest\n       of the line went to the next one without the prefix and left an\n       empty NOTE line behind (seen in a log of RAG - Register Setup). */\n    data _null_;\n        length summary $ 6000 part $ 500 line $ 520;\n        summary = symget(\"_rgls_summary\");\n        putLog \"NOTE: ----- RAG - List Documents -----\";\n        do i = 1 to countw(summary, \"|\");\n            part = strip(scan(summary, i, \"|\"));\n            line = \"NOTE:   \" || part;\n            if part ne \"\" then putLog line;\n        end;\n    run;\n%mend _rgls_status;\n%_rgls_status;"}, "type": "code", "ui": "{\n\t\"showPageContentOnly\": true,\n\t\"pages\": [\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t\"id\": \"pageDefinition\",\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"page\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"Definition\",\n\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgls_info\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Crawls the folder holding your documents - on the compute server file system or in SAS Content - fingerprints every document and diffs it against the incremental-ingestion ledger (<project>_LEDGER). Only new and changed documents flow further down the RAG ingestion flow.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgls_sourcePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"path\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Document folder (compute server file system or SAS Content):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"pathtype\": \"folder\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgls_ragProject\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"RAG project name (prefix of every pipeline table, max 20 characters):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"e.g. RAG_HR\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgls_tablesCaslib\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Caslib where the pipeline tables are stored:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgls_pipelineVersion\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Pipeline version stamped on every document (change it, e.g. v1 to v2, to re-ingest the whole corpus):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgls_includeCode\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"dropdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Source-code files (.py, .sas, .r, .js, .sql, ...):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"items\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"0\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Skip them (listed as skipped, with the reason)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"1\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Ingest them as plain text\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t],\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgls_sectionAdvanced\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Runtime\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgls_ragCorePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"path\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SAS Content folder holding rag_core (set by the deployment - not editable here):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"pathtype\": \"folder\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"enabled\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"$_rgls_ragCorePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"=\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"__set_by_deployment__\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgls_inventory\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"outputtable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Document inventory output:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t\"id\": \"pageAbout\",\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"page\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"About\",\n\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textAbout\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"RAG - List Documents step\\n==========\\n\\nCrawls a document source and diffs it against the ledger: unchanged documents are skipped downstream, previously failed documents re-enter the pipeline, documents that disappeared are marked deleted so the Load step removes their chunks. Filesystem documents are fingerprinted with a streaming SHA-256; SAS Content documents by the file's ETag (SAS Content issues a new one on every change), which avoids downloading the whole corpus twice per run. The ledger is the promoted CAS table <project>_LEDGER, written by the Load step (promote + save).\\n\\nFlow wiring: chain the document INVENTORY through every step - RAG - List Documents \u2192 Extract Text \u2192 Chunk Documents \u2192 Embed Chunks \u2192 Load Vector Store. The bulk data travels beside the flow in promoted CAS tables named <project>_ELEMENTS, <project>_CHUNKS, <project>_EMBEDDED and <project>_LEDGER in the tables caslib (each saved to disk, so state survives server restarts; names stay within 32 characters so they display nicely in SAS Studio). Each step's output table lands in that same caslib as <project>_INV_LIST, _INV_EXTRACT, _INV_CHUNK, _INV_EMBED and <project>_LOAD_REPORT unless you point the output port somewhere else. Give every step the SAME project name and caslib.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionPrereqs\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Pre-requisites\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textPrereqs\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Tested on SAS Viya 2026 (Stable).\\n\\n* The rag_core runtime must be deployed to SAS Content (default: /SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core) with deploy-rag-content.ps1/.sh - keep that folder read-only for regular users.\\n* The compute context's Python needs the requests, swat and pandas packages (swat/pandas carry the pipeline tables to CAS - varchar columns, no 32k limit).\\n* CAS available; the runner needs write access to the tables caslib.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionDocumentation\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Documentation\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textDocumentation\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"The step refuses to run while a scheduled ingestion job holds a fresh run lock on the same ledger (locks older than 30 minutes are considered stale).\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionChangelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Changelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textChangelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"* Version: 1.4 (20OCT2026)\\n      - A quotation mark, a percent sign, an ampersand or a semicolon of a message in the log or of the run summary is written as a character that reads the same - an apostrophe and a quotation mark as a backtick, a percent sign as pct, an ampersand as +, a semicolon as a comma. Version 1.3 wrote a blank in its place: RAG - Chunk Documents wrote the setup s 256-token chunk window x 85  safety margin (seen on 2026-10-20)\\n* Version: 1.3 (11OCT2026)\\n      - The run lock is declared the way the ledger holds its text columns - CHAR after the single-program ingestion job, VARCHAR after a flow - because CAS refuses a row whose column types differ from the table's\\n      - A ledger with CHAR columns is read without the blanks CAS pads them with\\n      - A ledger (<project>_LEDGER) that was saved but is not in memory - which is how a restart of the CAS server leaves it - is loaded back from its saved file before the run lock asks for its column types. The step used to read no previous run then, classify every document as new and start a new ledger. A saved file that cannot be loaded fails the step. Measured on SAS Viya 2026.09 with pgvector, with the saved ledger dropped from memory and not with a restarted CAS server: the step loaded a CHAR and a VARCHAR ledger back, took its run lock and listed every document as unchanged\\n      - Where the files of the caslib cannot be listed, a table that is not in memory cannot be looked for among them: the run goes on and says so in a WARNING, with what a ledger that is not in memory then means - every document counts as new and is embedded again. Measured on SAS Viya 2026.09 for the wording, with the ledger in a caslib of the CAS session whose files could not be listed: the step wrote the two WARNING lines and went on to its run lock, which such a caslib cannot hold\\n      - A step that fails also sets RAG_JOB_FAILED, a flag no step clears. A job that RAG - Register Setup generates from a flow reads it at its end, because RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED is cleared again by a later RAG - List Documents, RAG - Purge Documents or RAG - Retrieve Context of the same flow. Measured on SAS Viya 2026.09 with pgvector: a job that RAG - Register Setup generated, in which this step failed, ended as failed in SAS Job Execution, with the ERROR line of that check in its log\\n      - The run summary is read with symget, so that a run that succeeds does not write the NOTE about a quoted string of more than 262 bytes above it. Measured on SAS Viya 2026.09: the log of a flow of RAG - List Documents, Extract Text, Chunk Documents, Embed Chunks and Load Vector Store holds no such NOTE\\n      - The ERROR line of a run that fails is put together from a message read with symget as well. Written as a quoted string, it had the same NOTE above it whenever the line was longer than 262 bytes (seen on SAS Viya 2026.09 in a failing run of this step). Measured on SAS Viya 2026.09 with this version of the step and a documents folder that does not exist: the ERROR line of 311 characters stood on three log lines, each typed as an error, with no such NOTE above it\\n      - A part of the summary that is longer than the log line is written with its NOTE prefix; it left an empty NOTE line behind and went on without the prefix\\n      - The run id ends in ten digits taken from a UUID. It ended in the process id of the SAS session (SYSJOBID), which does not tell two sessions apart: it was 344 in twelve flow runs on SAS Viya 2026.09, each in a compute server of its own. Measured on SAS Viya 2026.09 with this version of the step: the ids of 28 runs of flows, purges and the ingestion job each ended in ten digits, no two alike\\n      - A step that fails hands the run lock back only when the lock row of its own run stands in the ledger. Without that row it leaves the ledger as it is and does not say that the run lock was released: a run that the lock of another run had refused, or whose ledger RAG - Load Vector Store had already written, rewrote and saved the ledger all the same. Measured on SAS Viya 2026.09 with this version of the step: a failing run took its own lock row out and said so, on a VARCHAR and on a CHAR ledger; a run that the lock of a running flow refused left the ledger and its file as they were and said nothing of a released lock\\n      - Where the ledger holds more than one lock row, the newest one decides whether another run holds the lock. One row was taken, whichever CAS returned first or last, so the lock row of a run that had crashed could hide the lock of a run that was at work. Measured on SAS Viya 2026.09 with a lock row older than 30 minutes and a fresh one, appended in either order: the step refused to run\\n* Version: 1.2 (29JUL2026)\\n      - SAS Content document sources; output tables land in the tables caslib; labelled columns; numeric and list-of-values fields; run summary in the log\\n* Version: 1.1 (28JUL2026)\\n      - Pipeline tables move to promoted CAS tables via SWAT (varchar, no 32k limit); automatic embed checkpoint\\n* Version: 1.0 (28JUL2026)\\n      - Initial version\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t}\n\t],\n\t\"syntaxversion\": \"1.3.0\",\n\t\"values\": {\n\t\t\"_rgls_ragCorePath\": \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core\",\n\t\t\"_rgls_ragProject\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgls_tablesCaslib\": \"casuser\",\n\t\t\"_rgls_sourcePath\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgls_pipelineVersion\": \"v1\"\n\t}\n}"}